{
 "what_this_is": "Ontology ids whose declared label does not match the term they resolve to, plus ids that do not resolve at all. RATCHET: `count` may only go DOWN. Fixing one means lowering it in the same commit.",
 "corpus_note": "`count` is only comparable against a run over the SAME corpus. If a source is added to EXISTENCE_ONLY or SCAN_SUFFIXES the count moves for a reason that is not a regression; record it here when it does.",
 "corpus": {
  "scan_suffixes": [
   ".json",
   ".jsonl",
   ".md",
   ".py",
   ".ts",
   ".tsx"
  ],
  "existence_only": [
   "MASTER_CROSSWALK.tsv"
  ]
 },
 "last_change": "Corpus grew, not a regression. A new problem kind, MALFORMED, was added 2026-09-07: a known prefix followed by something that is not an accession. 23 of them ship - 20 'chebi:<word>' placeholders in the participants lists of biochemical_mechanisms.py, nutrient_compound.py, do_calculus.py, causal_inference.py and causal_join_graph.py, plus 3 '<PREFIX>:illustrative' in agents/assay/ontology_stub.py. These were invisible, not passing: the CURIE regex requires four digits, so a placeholder was never resolved and never counted as unchecked. They matter because they occupy the ChEBI slot of the food -> chemical -> GO chain, so the join key that chain declares does not resolve to a molecule. Pattern is ':' only: allowing the OBO '_' form harvested 44 python identifiers (bfo_stack_ontology, chebi_local, uberon_hint) as false positives. Lowercase-with-digits stays valid - chebi:15637 is what normalize_crosswalk.py emits and what FDP-1 section 2 accepts.",
 "as_of": "2026-09-07",
